{"title":"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The shaded region below is called a shark's fin falcata, a figure studied by Leonardo da Vinci. It is bounded by the portion of the circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> that lies in the first quadrant, the portion of the circle with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/5/85524016576d4135def3798324635e6abd32e4fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"9\" height=\"21\" /> and center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/a/e5ac44e0478296923ce638e4b89795e761f25efc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,\\tfrac{3}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"21\" /> that lies in the first quadrant, and the line segment from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/f/7af424ab2c41e93a9e7ab081dee423809b2ba735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. What is the area of the shark's fin falcata?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce4e98a2133efe32043ca2e707377730ddad63c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import cse5;pathpen=black;pointpen=black; size(1.5inch); D(MP(&quot;x&quot;,(3.5,0),S)--(0,0)--MP(&quot;\\frac{3}{2}&quot;,(0,3/2),W)--MP(&quot;y&quot;,(0,3.5),W)); path P=(0,0)--MP(&quot;3&quot;,(3,0),S)..(3*dir(45))..MP(&quot;3&quot;,(0,3),W)--(0,3)..(3/2,3/2)..cycle; draw(P,linewidth(2)); fill(P,gray); [/asy]\" width=\"182\" height=\"182\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/a/03a66da142f0008a47b442fc8142e3614a3e48ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\dfrac{4\\pi}{5} \\qquad\\textbf{(B) } \\dfrac{9\\pi}{8} \\qquad\\textbf{(C) } \\dfrac{4\\pi}{3} \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } \\dfrac{7\\pi}{5} \\qquad\\textbf{(E) } \\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"427\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the shark's fin falcata is just the area of the quarter-circle minus the area of the semicircle. The quarter-circle has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> so it has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/e/07ea867fa55ecb191f9a1b579700059bed4dc186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{9\\pi}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"38\" />. The semicircle has radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/c/67ce01cd97c81718e787d0abf8093ec9dfc01b05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" /> so it has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/7/b774acf584027d9922727c6b1b1e213eb74cc461.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{9\\pi}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"22\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, the shaded area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/8/5e8ee44330e0c8fb74a918149818b4a59ff8d347.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{9\\pi}{4}-\\dfrac{9\\pi}{8}=\\boxed{\\mathbf{(B)}\\ \\dfrac{9\\pi}{8}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"165\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can reflect the figure four times to create a big circle with 2 small circles inside. We then know that the area of the 2 circles is half of the area of the big circle, meaning that the area of the 2 circles are equal to the area of the region in the big circle, but outside the small circle. Therefore the \"Shark Fin\" is just half of the area of the quarter-circle. We can fin the area of the quarter circle as stated above, and it is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/e/07ea867fa55ecb191f9a1b579700059bed4dc186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{9\\pi}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"38\" />. Then the area of the shark fin is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/7/b774acf584027d9922727c6b1b1e213eb74cc461.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{9\\pi}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"22\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~Fib_0112358 \nCan somebody polish this?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4fTjISCoRlU\">https://youtu.be/4fTjISCoRlU</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/22AUHebZNyk\">https://youtu.be/22AUHebZNyk</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B\">2015 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2015 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"